<entry xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xml:base="https://spec-kitty.github.io/doc-kitty/guides/markua-footnotes-showcase/">
  <id>https://spec-kitty.github.io/doc-kitty/guides/markua-footnotes-showcase/</id>
  <title>Markua footnotes showcase</title>
  <updated>2026-10-13T00:00:00.000Z</updated>
  <author><name>DocKitty Example</name></author>
  <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://spec-kitty.github.io/doc-kitty/guides/markua-footnotes-showcase/"/>
  <summary>Markua double-caret footnotes rendered as real, back-linked GFM footnotes (FR-004).</summary>
  <content type="html">

&lt;span id=&quot;markua-footnotes-showcase&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Markua writes footnotes with a &lt;strong&gt;double caret&lt;/strong&gt; — a reference marker &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;[^^N_M]&lt;/code&gt; in
the prose and a definition line &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;[^^N_M]:&lt;/code&gt; below. With the &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;markua&lt;/code&gt; preset on, the
&lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;markua-footnotes&lt;/code&gt; pass normalises the marker &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;remark-gfm&lt;/code&gt; already parsed so the
footnote renders as a real, numbered, back-linked note with a clean anchor id.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;a-single-footnote&quot;&gt;A single footnote&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rhetoric is the counterpart of dialectic&lt;sup&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#user-content-fn-0_1&quot; id=&quot;user-content-fnref-0_1&quot; data-footnote-ref=&quot;&quot; aria-describedby=&quot;footnote-label&quot;&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;, as Aristotle opens Book I.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;several-footnotes-in-order&quot;&gt;Several footnotes, in order&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The three kinds of rhetoric are deliberative&lt;sup&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#user-content-fn-0_2&quot; id=&quot;user-content-fnref-0_2&quot; data-footnote-ref=&quot;&quot; aria-describedby=&quot;footnote-label&quot;&gt;2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;, forensic&lt;sup&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#user-content-fn-0_3&quot; id=&quot;user-content-fnref-0_3&quot; data-footnote-ref=&quot;&quot; aria-describedby=&quot;footnote-label&quot;&gt;3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;, and
epideictic&lt;sup&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#user-content-fn-0_4&quot; id=&quot;user-content-fnref-0_4&quot; data-footnote-ref=&quot;&quot; aria-describedby=&quot;footnote-label&quot;&gt;4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; — each addressing a different hearer and a different time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;one-definition-referenced-twice&quot;&gt;One definition, referenced twice&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The enthymeme&lt;sup&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#user-content-fn-1_1&quot; id=&quot;user-content-fnref-1_1&quot; data-footnote-ref=&quot;&quot; aria-describedby=&quot;footnote-label&quot;&gt;5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; is the body of proof; the orator returns to the
enthymeme&lt;sup&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#user-content-fn-1_1&quot; id=&quot;user-content-fnref-1_1-2&quot; data-footnote-ref=&quot;&quot; aria-describedby=&quot;footnote-label&quot;&gt;5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; as the rhetorical counterpart of the syllogism.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;a-footnote-marker-inside-inline-code-stays-literal&quot;&gt;A footnote marker inside inline code stays literal&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The source spelling &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;[^^0_1]&lt;/code&gt; is shown here verbatim inside a code span, so it is
NOT turned into a footnote — only prose markers become notes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;section data-footnotes=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;footnotes&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;sr-only&quot; id=&quot;footnote-label&quot;&gt;Footnotes&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li id=&quot;user-content-fn-0_1&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;“The counterpart of dialectic” — Rhetoric I.1, 1354a. &lt;a href=&quot;#user-content-fnref-0_1&quot; data-footnote-backref=&quot;&quot; aria-label=&quot;Back to reference 1&quot; class=&quot;data-footnote-backref&quot;&gt;↩&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li id=&quot;user-content-fn-0_2&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deliberative rhetoric concerns the future: exhortation and dissuasion. &lt;a href=&quot;#user-content-fnref-0_2&quot; data-footnote-backref=&quot;&quot; aria-label=&quot;Back to reference 2&quot; class=&quot;data-footnote-backref&quot;&gt;↩&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li id=&quot;user-content-fn-0_3&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Forensic (judicial) rhetoric concerns the past: accusation and defence. &lt;a href=&quot;#user-content-fnref-0_3&quot; data-footnote-backref=&quot;&quot; aria-label=&quot;Back to reference 3&quot; class=&quot;data-footnote-backref&quot;&gt;↩&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li id=&quot;user-content-fn-0_4&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Epideictic (ceremonial) rhetoric concerns the present: praise and blame. &lt;a href=&quot;#user-content-fnref-0_4&quot; data-footnote-backref=&quot;&quot; aria-label=&quot;Back to reference 4&quot; class=&quot;data-footnote-backref&quot;&gt;↩&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li id=&quot;user-content-fn-1_1&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The enthymeme is a rhetorical syllogism drawn from probabilities and signs. &lt;a href=&quot;#user-content-fnref-1_1&quot; data-footnote-backref=&quot;&quot; aria-label=&quot;Back to reference 5&quot; class=&quot;data-footnote-backref&quot;&gt;↩&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;#user-content-fnref-1_1-2&quot; data-footnote-backref=&quot;&quot; aria-label=&quot;Back to reference 5-2&quot; class=&quot;data-footnote-backref&quot;&gt;↩&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;</content>
